  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A thin uniform equilateral plate rests in a vertical plane with one of its vertex&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> on a rough horizontal floor and another vertex&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;on a smooth vertical wall. If the coefficient of friction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>, then the least angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>θ</mi></math> its base&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math> can make with the horizontal surface is</p>\r\r<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0117_42ec85176a03.jpeg\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 175px;\" /></p>\r"
  },
